# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Overview {#overview}"
msgstr "Pangkalahatang-ideya {#overview}"

# doq: mechanical transfer from the previous translation
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Fire Opal Performance Management makes it simple for anyone to achieve meaningful results from quantum computers at scale without needing to be quantum hardware experts. When running circuits with Fire Opal Performance Management, AI-driven error suppression techniques are automatically applied, enabling the scaling of larger problems with more gates and qubits. This approach reduces the number of shots required to reach the correct answer, with no added overhead, resulting in significant savings in both compute time and cost.\n"
msgstr "Ginagawa ng Fire Opal Performance Management na simple para sa sinuman na makamit ang makabuluhang resulta mula sa mga quantum computer sa malaking sukat nang hindi kailangang maging eksperto sa quantum hardware. Kapag nagpapatakbo ng mga circuit gamit ang Fire Opal Performance Management, awtomatikong inilalapat ang mga AI-driven na teknik ng error suppression, na nagbibigay-daan sa pag-scale ng mas malalaking problema na may mas maraming gate at qubit. Binabawasan ng approach na ito ang bilang ng mga shot na kailangan para makamit ang tamang sagot, nang walang dagdag na overhead — na nagresulta sa malaking tipid sa oras ng computation at gastos.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Performance Management suppresses errors and increases the probability of getting the correct answer on noisy hardware. In other words, it increases the signal-to-noise ratio. The following image shows how increased accuracy enabled by Performance Management can reduce the need for additional shots in the case of a 10-qubit Quantum Fourier Transform algorithm. With only 30 shots, Q-CTRL reaches the 99% confidence threshold, whereas the default (`QiskitRuntime` Sampler, `optimization_level`=3 and `resilience_level`=1, `ibm_sherbrooke`) requires 170,000 shots. By getting the right answer faster, you save significant compute runtime.\n"
msgstr "Sinusupress ng Performance Management ang mga error at pinapataas ang posibilidad na makuha ang tamang sagot sa maingay na hardware. Sa madaling salita, pinapataas nito ang signal-to-noise ratio. Ipinapakita ng sumusunod na larawan kung paano maaaring bawasan ng mas mataas na katumpakan na pinapagana ng Performance Management ang pangangailangan para sa karagdagang mga shot sa kaso ng isang 10-qubit Quantum Fourier Transform algorithm. Sa 30 shot lamang, naabot ng Q-CTRL ang 99% confidence threshold, samantalang ang default (`QiskitRuntime` Sampler, `optimization_level`=3 at `resilience_level`=1, `ibm_sherbrooke`) ay nangangailangan ng 170,000 shot. Sa pamamagitan ng pagkuha ng tamang sagot nang mas mabilis, makakatipid ka ng malaking oras ng computation.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Visualization of the improved runtime](/docs/images/guides/qctrl-performance-management/achieve_more.svg)\n"
msgstr "![Visualization ng pinahusay na runtime](/docs/images/guides/qctrl-performance-management/achieve_more.svg)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Performance Management function can be used with any algorithm, and you can easily use it in place of the standard [IBM Quantum primitives](/guides/qiskit-runtime-primitives). Behind the scenes, multiple error suppression techniques work together to prevent errors from happening at runtime. All Fire Opal pipeline methods are pre-configured and algorithm-agnostic, meaning you always get the best performance out of the box.\n"
msgstr "Maaaring gamitin ang Performance Management function sa anumang algorithm, at madali mo itong magagamit bilang kapalit ng mga standard na [IBM Quantum primitives](/guides/qiskit-runtime-primitives). Sa likod ng eksena, maraming teknik ng error suppression ang nagtatrabaho nang sabay-sabay upang maiwasan ang mga error sa runtime. Lahat ng Fire Opal pipeline method ay pre-configured at algorithm-agnostic, ibig sabihin palagi kang makakakuha ng pinakamahusay na performance nang walang karagdagang configuration.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To get access to Performance Management, [contact Q-CTRL](https://form.typeform.com/to/uOAVDnGg?typeform-source=q-ctrl.com).\n"
msgstr "Para makakuha ng access sa Performance Management, [makipag-ugnayan sa Q-CTRL](https://form.typeform.com/to/uOAVDnGg?typeform-source=q-ctrl.com).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Description {#description}"
msgstr "Paglalarawan {#description}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Fire Opal Performance Management has two options for execution that are similar to the IBM Quantum primitives, so you can easily swap in the Q-CTRL Sampler and Estimator. The general workflow for using the Performance Management function is:\n"
"1. Define your circuit (and operators in the case of the Estimator).\n"
"2. Run the circuit.\n"
"3. Retrieve the results.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang Fire Opal Performance Management ay may dalawang opsyon para sa pagpapatakbo na katulad ng mga IBM Quantum primitives, kaya madali mong mapapalitan ng Q-CTRL Sampler at Estimator. Ang pangkalahatang workflow para sa paggamit ng Performance Management function ay:\n"
"1. Tukuyin ang iyong circuit (at mga operator sa kaso ng Estimator).\n"
"2. Patakbuhin ang circuit.\n"
"3. Kunin ang mga resulta.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To reduce hardware noise, Fire Opal employs a range of AI-driven error suppression techniques depicted in the following image. With Fire Opal, the entire pipeline is completely automated with zero need for configuration.\n"
msgstr "Para bawasan ang ingay ng hardware, gumagamit ang Fire Opal ng iba't ibang AI-driven na teknik ng error suppression na ipinapakita sa sumusunod na larawan. Sa Fire Opal, ang buong pipeline ay ganap na automated nang walang pangangailangan para sa configuration.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Fire Opal's pipeline eliminates the need for additional overhead, such as increased quantum runtime or extra physical qubits. Note that classical processing time remains a factor (refer to the [Benchmarks](#benchmarks) section for estimates, where \"Total time\" reflects both classical and quantum processing). In contrast to error mitigation, which requires overhead in the form of sampling, Fire Opal's error suppression works at both the gate and pulse levels to address various sources of noise and to prevent the likelihood of an error occurring. By preventing errors, the need for expensive post-processing is eliminated.\n"
msgstr "Inaalis ng pipeline ng Fire Opal ang pangangailangan para sa karagdagang overhead, tulad ng karagdagang quantum runtime o dagdag na pisikal na qubit. Tandaan na ang classical processing time ay nananatiling isang salik (sumangguni sa seksyon ng [Mga Benchmark](#benchmarks) para sa mga pagtatantya, kung saan ang \"Total time\" ay sumasalamin sa parehong classical at quantum processing). Kumpara sa error mitigation, na nangangailangan ng overhead sa anyo ng sampling, ang error suppression ng Fire Opal ay gumagana sa parehong gate at pulse na antas upang tugunan ang iba't ibang pinagkukunan ng ingay at upang maiwasan ang posibilidad ng paglitaw ng error. Sa pamamagitan ng pag-iwas sa mga error, naaalis ang pangangailangan para sa mahal na post-processing.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The following image depicts the error suppression methods automated by Fire Opal Performance Management.\n"
msgstr "Ipinapakita ng sumusunod na larawan ang mga paraan ng error suppression na na-automate ng Fire Opal Performance Management.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Visualization of the error suppression pipeline](/docs/images/guides/qctrl-performance-management/error_suppression.svg)\n"
msgstr "![Visualization ng error suppression pipeline](/docs/images/guides/qctrl-performance-management/error_suppression.svg)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The function offers two primitives, Sampler and Estimator, and the inputs and outputs of both extend the implemented spec for [IBM Quantum V2 primitives](/guides/primitive-input-output#pubs). To access results from previous runs, see [how to retrieve previous quantum function jobs](/guides/functions-get-started#list-previously-run-functions-jobs).\n"
msgstr "Nag-aalok ang function ng dalawang primitive, Sampler at Estimator, at ang mga input at output ng pareho ay nagpapalawak ng implemented spec para sa [IBM Quantum V2 primitives](/guides/primitive-input-output#pubs). Para ma-access ang mga resulta mula sa mga nakaraang run, tingnan ang [kung paano kunin ang mga nakaraang quantum function job](/guides/functions-get-started#list-previously-run-functions-jobs).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Benchmarks {#benchmarks}"
msgstr "Mga Benchmark {#benchmarks}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[Published algorithmic benchmarking](https://journals.aps.org/prapplied/abstract/10.1103/PhysRevApplied.20.024034) results demonstrate significant performance improvement across various algorithms, including Bernstein-Vazirani, quantum Fourier transform, Grover’s search, quantum approximate optimization algorithm, and variational quantum eigensolver. The rest of this section provides more details about types of algorithms you can run, as well as the expected performance and runtimes.\n"
msgstr "Ang mga resulta ng [nai-publish na algorithmic benchmarking](https://journals.aps.org/prapplied/abstract/10.1103/PhysRevApplied.20.024034) ay nagpapakita ng makabuluhang pagpapabuti ng performance sa iba't ibang algorithm, kabilang ang Bernstein-Vazirani, quantum Fourier transform, Grover's search, quantum approximate optimization algorithm, at variational quantum eigensolver. Ang natitirang bahagi ng seksyong ito ay nagbibigay ng karagdagang detalye tungkol sa mga uri ng algorithm na maaari mong patakbuhin, pati na rin ang inaasahang performance at mga runtime.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The following independent studies demonstrate how Q-CTRL's Performance Management enables algorithmic research at record-breaking scale:\n"
"- [Parametrized Energy-Efficient Quantum Kernels for Network Service Fault Diagnosis](https://arxiv.org/abs/2405.09724v1) - up to 50-qubit quantum kernel learning\n"
"- [Tensor-based quantum phase difference estimation for large-scale demonstration](https://arxiv.org/abs/2408.04946) - up to 33-qubit quantum phase estimation\n"
"- [Hierarchical Learning for Quantum ML: Novel Training Technique for Large-Scale Variational Quantum Circuits](https://arxiv.org/abs/2311.12929) - up to 21-qubit quantum data loading\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang mga sumusunod na independyenteng pag-aaral ay nagpapakita kung paano pinapagana ng Performance Management ng Q-CTRL ang algorithmic na pananaliksik sa record-breaking na sukat:\n"
"- [Parametrized Energy-Efficient Quantum Kernels for Network Service Fault Diagnosis](https://arxiv.org/abs/2405.09724v1) - hanggang 50-qubit quantum kernel learning\n"
"- [Tensor-based quantum phase difference estimation for large-scale demonstration](https://arxiv.org/abs/2408.04946) - hanggang 33-qubit quantum phase estimation\n"
"- [Hierarchical Learning for Quantum ML: Novel Training Technique for Large-Scale Variational Quantum Circuits](https://arxiv.org/abs/2311.12929) - hanggang 21-qubit quantum data loading\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The following table provides a rough guide on accuracy and runtimes from prior benchmarking runs on `ibm_fez`. Performance on other devices may vary. The usage time is based on an assumption of 10,000 shots per circuit. The \"Number of qubits\" indicated is not a hard limitation but represents rough thresholds where you can expect extremely consistent solution accuracy. Larger problem sizes have been successfully solved, and testing beyond these limits is encouraged.\n"
msgstr "Ang sumusunod na talahanayan ay nagbibigay ng magaspang na gabay sa katumpakan at mga runtime mula sa mga nakaraang benchmarking run sa `ibm_fez`. Ang performance sa ibang device ay maaaring magkaiba. Ang oras ng paggamit ay batay sa assumption na 10,000 shot bawat circuit. Ang \"Bilang ng mga qubit\" na ipinahiwatig ay hindi isang mahigpit na limitasyon kundi kumakatawan sa tantiyang mga threshold kung saan maaari kang umasa ng napaka-consistent na katumpakan ng solusyon. Matagumpay na nalutas ang mas malalaking sukat ng problema, at hinihikayat ang pagsubok na higit pa sa mga limitasyong ito.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"| Example    | Number of qubits | Accuracy | Measure of accuracy | Total time (s) | Runtime usage (s) | Primitive (Mode) |\n"
"| ---------  | ---------------- | -------------------------- | -------- | ---------- | ------------- |------------- |\n"
"| Bernstein–Vazirani  |  50Q    | 100%  | Success Rate (Percentage of runs where the correct answer is the highest count bitstring)     | 10    | 8         | Sampler |\n"
"| Quantum Fourier Transform | 30Q              | 100% | Success Rate (Percentage of runs where the correct answer is the highest count bitstring)      | 10    | 8        | Sampler |\n"
"| Quantum Phase Estimation  | 30Q   | 99.9998%  | Accuracy of the angle found: `1- abs(real_angle - angle_found)/pi`  | 10  | 8  | Sampler |\n"
"| Quantum simulation: Ising model (15 steps) | 20Q  | 99.775%   |  $A$ (defined below)  |  60 (per step)  | 15 (per step)   | Estimator |\n"
"| Quantum simulation 2: molecular dynamics (20 time points) | 34Q  |  96.78%  |  $A_{mean}$ (defined below)   | 10 (per time point)    | 6 (per time point)  | Estimator |\n"
msgstr ""
"| Halimbawa    | Bilang ng qubit | Katumpakan | Sukatan ng katumpakan | Kabuuang oras (s) | Paggamit ng runtime (s) | Primitive (Mode) |\n"
"| ---------  | ---------------- | -------------------------- | -------- | ---------- | ------------- |------------- |\n"
"| Bernstein–Vazirani  |  50Q    | 100%  | Success Rate (Porsyento ng mga run kung saan ang tamang sagot ang bitstring na may pinakamataas na bilang)     | 10    | 8         | Sampler |\n"
"| Quantum Fourier Transform | 30Q              | 100% | Success Rate (Porsyento ng mga run kung saan ang tamang sagot ang bitstring na may pinakamataas na bilang)      | 10    | 8        | Sampler |\n"
"| Quantum Phase Estimation  | 30Q   | 99.9998%  | Katumpakan ng nahanap na anggulo: `1- abs(real_angle - angle_found)/pi`  | 10  | 8  | Sampler |\n"
"| Quantum simulation: Ising model (15 hakbang) | 20Q  | 99.775%   |  $A$ (tinukoy sa ibaba)  |  60 (bawat hakbang)  | 15 (bawat hakbang)   | Estimator |\n"
"| Quantum simulation 2: molecular dynamics (20 time point) | 34Q  |  96.78%  |  $A_{mean}$ (tinukoy sa ibaba)   | 10 (bawat time point)    | 6 (bawat time point)  | Estimator |\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Defining the accuracy of the measurement of an expectation value - the metric $A$ is defined as follows:\n"
"$$\n"
"A = 1 - \\frac{|\\epsilon^{ideal} - \\epsilon^{meas}|}{\\epsilon^{ideal}_{max} - \\epsilon^{ideal}_{min}},\n"
"$$\n"
"where $ \\epsilon^{ideal} $ = ideal expectation value,  $ \\epsilon^{meas} $ = measured expectation value, $\\epsilon^{ideal}_{max} $ = ideal maximum value, and $\\epsilon^{ideal}_{min}$ = ideal minimum value. $A_{mean}$ is simply the average of the value of $A$ across multiple measurements.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pagtukoy ng katumpakan ng pagsukat ng expectation value — ang metric na $A$ ay tinukoy tulad ng sumusunod:\n"
"$$\n"
"A = 1 - \\frac{|\\epsilon^{ideal} - \\epsilon^{meas}|}{\\epsilon^{ideal}_{max} - \\epsilon^{ideal}_{min}},\n"
"$$\n"
"kung saan ang $ \\epsilon^{ideal} $ = ideal na expectation value, $ \\epsilon^{meas} $ = nasukat na expectation value, $\\epsilon^{ideal}_{max} $ = ideal na maximum value, at $\\epsilon^{ideal}_{min}$ = ideal na minimum value. Ang $A_{mean}$ ay simpleng average ng halaga ng $A$ sa maraming pagsukat.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This metric is used because it is invariant to global shifts and scaling in the range of attainable values. In other words, regardless of whether you shift the range of possible expectation values higher or lower or increase the spread, the value of $A$ should remain consistent.\n"
msgstr "Ginagamit ang metric na ito dahil ito ay invariant sa mga global shift at scaling sa hanay ng mga maaabot na halaga. Sa madaling salita, anuman ang itaas o ibaba mo ang hanay ng mga posibleng expectation value o palawakin ang pagkakalat, dapat manatiling consistent ang halaga ng $A$.\n"

